### A1. Multi-user git ownership / DAC (KNOWN BREAKAGE)

Problem (audited): VE monorepo `.git` top is dlang:ai-shared 2770, but bulk of
objects/refs/logs/HEAD/config are dlang:ai-code (often 660/2775 setgid). ai-planner is
in ai-shared NOT ai-code → cannot read HEAD/config → git log/status fail (Unix, not
Landlock). remotetable/extractmail already OK; orchestration-example wrong model
(ai-code / incomplete setgid).

Requirements:
1) Repair VE common `.git` to documented model (docs/reference/MULTIUSER_GIT_VE_PARITY.md):
   - group ai-shared recursively on .git
   - every directory under .git: 2770 setgid
   - core.sharedRepository=group
   - HEAD/config/packed-refs/refs/logs metadata ug+rw for group
2) Repair orchestration-example the same way (under GIT_HOME).
3) Re-audit remotetable + extractmail (expect already OK; fix if drifted).
4) Land fix scripts in-tree if not committed: fix-multiuser-git-hosts.sh,
   fix-ve-git-shared.sh (or equivalent). Prefer one SoT script; wrappers OK.
5) Prove as non-interactive checks where possible:
   - paths not group ai-shared under .git: 0 (or documented residual)
   - dirs without setgid under .git: 0
   - simulated or real: ai-planner can read HEAD + config + run `git log -1`
     (sudo -u ai-planner … when available; else DAC simulation + dlang-runbook)
6) Root-cause note in evidence: setgid ai-code on objects/refs + ongoing commits
   re-infect; partial chgrp of .git top only is insufficient. Prevention note:
   set-worktree-perms / ops must not leave common .git children on ai-code.

